# 📊 Day 079 — Factors for Nudge Presentation

## 🎯 Objective
- Prepare a business-analysis presentation around factors affecting nudge response.
- Separate intervention variables from response variables.
- Compare click and conversion behaviour.
- Organise factor analysis into a presentation-ready workflow.

## 🧩 Case Context
- This package uses a synthetic e-commerce nudge dataset.
- It is created for Business Data Management practice.
- It is not official IIT Madras data.
- It is not real PayBuddy or market data.

## 🔍 Factors Covered
- Nudge type.
- Customer segment.
- Region.
- Device.
- Product category.

## 📈 Outcomes
- Nudge exposure.
- Click response.
- Purchase response.
- Order value.
- Repeat visit.

## 🧮 Key Measures
- Click rate.
- Conversion rate.
- Repeat-visit rate.
- Average order value.
- Lift versus default reference.

## 📂 Workbook Structure
- Nudge_Factor_Data stores observations.
- Nudge_Factor_Summary compares nudge types.
- Customer_Segment_Summary analyses segments.
- Region_Summary analyses regions.
- Device_Summary analyses devices.
- Category_Summary analyses categories.
- Nudge_KPIs contains headline metrics.
- Factor_Definitions defines analytical factors.
- Presentation_Stages provides presentation flow.
- Analysis_Questions contains business questions.
- Business_Insights stores descriptive observations.
- Data_Dictionary documents fields.
- Nudge_Factor_Presentation_Dashboard contains prepared charts.

## 📊 Dashboard
- Conversion Rate by Nudge Type.
- Lift versus Default Reference.
- Conversion Rate by Customer Segment.
- Conversion Rate by Device.

## 🐍 Python Analysis
- Reads the workbook.
- Creates derived measures.
- Aggregates factor summaries.
- Calculates baseline lift.
- Exports CSV files.
- Generates presentation charts.

## ⚠️ Interpretation Rule
- A difference between groups is descriptive.
- It does not by itself prove causality.
- Experimental design matters when making causal claims.
- Denominators should always be shown with rates.

## 🏅 Badges
- 📊 Business Analytics.
- 🧩 Factor Analysis.
- 🛒 E-Commerce.
- 📗 Excel.
- 🐍 Python.
- 🎤 Presentation.

## ✅ Completion Checklist
- Dataset prepared.
- Factor summaries prepared.
- Baseline defined.
- Segment analysis prepared.
- Dashboard prepared.
- Python outputs generated.
- Presentation questions documented.
- Business limitations documented.

## 📌 Presentation Deliverables
- Business question slide.
- Dataset and factor-definition slide.
- Baseline comparison slide.
- Factor comparison charts.
- Segment and device analysis.
- Evidence and limitation slide.
- Final discussion points.

## 🔁 Reproducibility
- The Excel workbook stores the prepared analytical tables.
- The Python script reproduces the main summary calculations.
- PNG outputs can be reused in presentation material.
- All figures are based on the synthetic learning dataset.